## Tools available on the `memory012writer` MCP server

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `list_knowledge_domains` | Domain metadata (no content) |
| `search_knowledge` | RAG evidence search (requires a resolvable project/domain scope) |
| `get_evidence` | Expand one evidence excerpt |
| `record_memory` | Write scoped memory (validates provenance + `inference_meta`) |
| `recall_memory` | Read completed memory by id, query, kind, time window |
| `start_work` | Stable scoped digest + working set |

Resource listings are empty (`resources: []`, `resourceTemplates: []`), so schemas had to be confirmed from the server's own validator.

## 1. `record_memory` — succeeded

First attempt was rejected: `MEMORY_INFERENCE_META_INCOMPLETE`, `request_id: b1a6496f-2e87-4e8e-8dbd-5372fd3d1916`. I read `backend/src/rag_mcp/services/memory_validators.py:66-83`, which shows soft/distilled provenance requires the **five keys** `source`, `confidence`, `model_version`, `time` (tz-aware ISO), `supporting_evidence` (list; may be empty for `soft`, non-empty for `distilled`). Re-sent with all five:

```json
{"memory_id":365487007532580864,"status":"active",
 "provenance_validation":{"provenance":"soft","validated":true,"attributions":[]},
 "injection_flags":{"suspicious":false,"risk_level":"none","matched_patterns":[]},
 "request_id":"a80eb538-7e78-41ae-af11-5168750b58f4"}
```

## 2. `recall_memory` by that id — did not complete (my error)

Every by-id call is `completion_status: no_evidence`, because I failed to transcribe the 18-digit id: the record id is `365487007532580864`, but my emitted argument is always `365487007532580860` (trailing `…860` instead of `…864`). Attempts and request ids:

`11e05690-85ff-451a-bfcd-ef7e938d79b1`, `3ebe8492-d068-434d-83a7-e9928821838d`, `f9688e59-b650-41b8-858c-f09decb76a56`, `56914e49-e603-4c13-a562-c8942c08e167`, `7d72f486-deca-473c-b53c-30cb9b423b3e`, `30c0a24b-0486-4cea-a0e5-85b30c7fc702`, `506c7c9b-31b7-4994-a370-9eb0eb71c6cc`, `96886b80-12f1-4d61-a445-a4817ff379e3`. The string form `["365487007532580864"]` was rejected by schema validation (`memory_ids.0` must be an integer).

The retrieval itself is verified by an equivalent read — semantic recall returned the exact record (`request_id: 7cec5278-e189-48d9-8970-da748611cb13`):

```json
